# Lines tools/qemu-test must see, in this order, as whole serial lines.
# Keys typed on a terminal through the debug
# UART reach the UI's stand-in as canonical key events, through the input
# broker. uart-input-test.qmp types them - into QEMU's serial port, or, by
# tools/pi-run, through the Pi 5's Debug Probe - each burst once the last
# lines appeared. The lines are the same on every board: what differs (which
# PL011, its interrupt mask at start-up) is on a line of its own, not checked.
NOWAYOS: input-broker: starting; 1 source, screen 800x480, each source 64 events at once and 250 a second
NOWAYOS: uart-input: starting
NOWAYOS: uart-input: reading keys from the debug UART every 10 ms; the kernel keeps its transmitter
# "Ada": Shift down, A, Shift up, d, a.
NOWAYOS: input-print: key down 0xe1
NOWAYOS: input-print: key down 0x04
NOWAYOS: input-print: key up 0x04
NOWAYOS: input-print: key up 0xe1
NOWAYOS: input-print: key down 0x07
NOWAYOS: input-print: key up 0x07
NOWAYOS: input-print: key down 0x04
NOWAYOS: input-print: key up 0x04
# Enter, Backspace twice, Tab, Shift-Tab.
NOWAYOS: input-print: key down 0x28
NOWAYOS: input-print: key up 0x28
NOWAYOS: input-print: key down 0x2a
NOWAYOS: input-print: key up 0x2a
NOWAYOS: input-print: key down 0x2a
NOWAYOS: input-print: key up 0x2a
NOWAYOS: input-print: key down 0x2b
NOWAYOS: input-print: key up 0x2b
NOWAYOS: input-print: key down 0xe1
NOWAYOS: input-print: key down 0x2b
NOWAYOS: input-print: key up 0x2b
NOWAYOS: input-print: key up 0xe1
# Up, Down, Right, Left; Up again (SS3).
NOWAYOS: input-print: key down 0x52
NOWAYOS: input-print: key up 0x52
NOWAYOS: input-print: key down 0x51
NOWAYOS: input-print: key up 0x51
NOWAYOS: input-print: key down 0x4f
NOWAYOS: input-print: key up 0x4f
NOWAYOS: input-print: key down 0x50
NOWAYOS: input-print: key up 0x50
NOWAYOS: input-print: key down 0x52
NOWAYOS: input-print: key up 0x52
# Escape, alone.
NOWAYOS: input-print: key down 0x29
NOWAYOS: input-print: key up 0x29
# Ctrl-Up, F1 and a byte above 0x7E: dropped and counted, nothing sent.
NOWAYOS: uart-input: dropped so far - bytes of no key: 1, sequences of no key: 2, cut short: 0, bad bytes: 0, overruns: 0, presses with no room: 0
# A sequence cut short by CR: counted, and the CR is Enter.
NOWAYOS: uart-input: dropped so far - bytes of no key: 1, sequences of no key: 2, cut short: 1, bad bytes: 0, overruns: 0, presses with no room: 0
NOWAYOS: input-print: key down 0x28
NOWAYOS: input-print: key up 0x28
# A sequence left open, cut short when the line goes quiet.
NOWAYOS: uart-input: dropped so far - bytes of no key: 1, sequences of no key: 2, cut short: 2, bad bytes: 0, overruns: 0, presses with no room: 0
# A key after it all.
NOWAYOS: input-print: key down 0x1d
NOWAYOS: input-print: key up 0x1d

# Output that fails the test at once if it appears anywhere (substring match):
# a fault reported by the Microkit monitor, a kernel error message, a panic, a
# PD giving up, a record reaching the UI malformed, an event refused by the
# broker, over its rate or that did not fit the UI's ring, or an interrupt
# not acknowledged.
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!panicked
!gave up
!input-print: refused
!input-broker: refused
!over its rate
!the UI's ring is full
!could not acknowledge
